# edge-click (M9): an edge marker clicked (CartesianPlane.test.tsx: "pans a point off the view into it
# when its edge marker is clicked"). On x³ (picked in the picker, its option (246.5, 164, 97.25 x 34)
# at 1440 x 900, on both surfaces), P at (2, 8) lies above the view's 7.92, so its marker
# "▲ P (2.00, 8.00)" sits on the top edge at P's x (M6's edge-x3; its plate about (970, 114.5)–(1141,
# 152) in the page, drawn on the canvas). The pointer on it, a press pans P in: along y, the axis it
# lies past, it lands a quarter of the plane in from the top edge, 198 px down (the pan's y −4.04,
# the origin from (468, 396) to (468, 598)); along x the view stays.
# Over an edge marker the plane names no mark, so Q follows the pointer there: at (2, 8) too, its own
# edge marker below P's; the shot waits out its 160 ms entrance on the reference (M10's motion).
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 300
click 295 181
move 760 48
wait 2000
move 1056 133
wait 500
shot over-edge
click 1056 133
wait 500
shot edge-clicked
